ing that climate change is real  and that humans may have a hand in it is  is tantamount to  buying into a certain ideology which  people are just not willing to do  even though he can see his farm is  directly impacted that's what's so  fascinating  right next to uh his farm his farmland  has essentially become a lake he's got 4  000 acres  80 percent of it is still underwater and  yet there's that reluctance to take that  one further step insane  are they linking those floods adam back  in march to climate change so scientists  won't  specifically point to any one storm and  say this is the direct result of climate  change but what they will say is look  climate is in fact changing  and that based on where we are these  like  these events are much more likely to  happen so this is as we would project  and they'll point to the fact that 100  year storms are happening now every five  to seven years  yeah wow the metaphor that always  brought it home for me is is uh the  weather is like a hand of cards  climate change is stacking the deck so  those hands are full of extreme weather  adam thank you very much eye opening  report as always we hope to see you back  soon  you can watch the latest cbsn originals  documentary a climate reckoning in the  heartland  right now it's streaming on cbsnews.com  heartland
 

